=== fixed-point lemma ===
  If P is G-invariant and P => Q = q* with Q(g m) = rho(g) Q(m), then rho(g) q* = q* for all admissible g.
  weight 1: solutions of lam^w q = q for generic lam: [0] (plus q = infinity)
  weight -1/2: solutions of lam^w q = q for generic lam: [0] (plus q = infinity)
  weight 2: solutions of lam^w q = q for generic lam: [0] (plus q = infinity)
  pin shift: lambda_0 + s = lambda_0 has no solution for s != 0 -> no finite lambda_0 selectable by T_s-invariant P
  => invariant P can only impose G-invariant sets: for a weight-w quantity {0}, (0,inf), {inf} and unions
     (sign/class statements), or exact values of weight-0 (G-invariant) combinations.
